f63b17f6768a" :answer-field/key "$m=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30a80f14-b653-5ec9-a12d-20d43bb40f91" :question/math-academy-id "q-128506" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nis $-29$, find all the possible values of $m.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-6\\begin{vmatrix}m & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+m\\begin{vmatrix}m & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3-0)-6(m-0)+m(m-6) \\\\  & =3-6m+{m}^{2}-6m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-12m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-29,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-12m+3 & =-29 \\\\ {m}^{2}-12m+32 & =0 \\\\ m & =\\frac{-(-12)\\pm \\sqrt{{12}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 32}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=4$ and $m=8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186600360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "047015d3-245d-57d8-9e76-8638640ecadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599996} {:answer/id #uuid "1739086c-31bb-5871-a79e-7dc7695e0ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600014} {:answer/id #uuid "2cba192d-7fa8-592e-8135-fb3dd84b80b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600042} {:answer/id #uuid "315ab749-9806-5ebd-8701-231f7b3657cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600049} {:answer/id #uuid "3be5ac37-072b-53ef-b802-b3646a736a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "047015d3-245d-57d8-9e76-8638640ecadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599996} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2bbd54c-6dcc-55cc-991a-9fa16098a05c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600319}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "388215dc-389a-56fb-9d33-97db6c17cf42" :question/math-academy-id "q-18249" :question/problem "Given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nand $det(D)=481,$ find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & x\\end{vmatrix}-6\\begin{vmatrix}-8 & 5 \\\\ 3 & x\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}-8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-5)-6\\cdot (-8x-15)+2\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =-25+48x+90-16 \\\\  & =48x+49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $481,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48x+49 & =481 \\\\ 48x & =432 \\\\ x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186600397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088ca494-dbe0-58cc-a825-9b36f7352e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600000} {:answer/id #uuid "18be830b-1ffb-5bf6-8377-7849fc987525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600017} {:answer/id #uuid "26c28228-3482-5c92-9704-6be2b24b3aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600032} {:answer/id #uuid "94dac9f4-9cec-5f26-a068-9bab6dec10a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600156} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f4e25f-e39c-59cb-8c19-a107f78ddf77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18be830b-1ffb-5bf6-8377-7849fc987525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600017} :answer-field/id #uuid "b385464f-8745-5852-b86e-bb292cb24e13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186600320}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5d8fd25-145e-5cde-b46d-30f32d959af5" :question/math-academy-id "q-18274" :question/problem "Given that $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ m & 1 & m \\\\ -1 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $det(B)=-50,$ find the value of $m.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ m & 1 & m \\\\ -1 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & m \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}m & m \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}m & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2-4m)+3\\cdot (-2m+m)-(4m+1) \\\\  & =-4-8m-3m-4m-1 \\\\  & =-5-15m\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-50,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5-15m & =-50 \\\\ -15m & =-45 \\\\ m & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643195b8-5f3c-5dec-a199-1d4e1566d7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636844} {:answer/id #uuid "ab69d199-b8fe-570c-872d-ce2b5bd7a3b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636969} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe6b9bb-289d-560f-a1f6-fa661bc9a8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636999} {:answer/id #uuid "db4125cf-daf8-57ba-ab40-6725dd625804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637051} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6a29d3-f315-52df-9f3d-fdc297bf21be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff6a29d3-f315-52df-9f3d-fdc297bf21be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637116} :answer-field/id #uuid "f566f2c2-8864-5e73-a36e-4bddc02ba233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637223}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b137dad-7db4-50cb-b5c8-f93f31b8129d" :question/math-academy-id "q-18253" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1-2p & 4 & 2p+1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nis $-126,$  find the value of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1-2p & 4 & 2p+1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =(1-2p)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-4\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(2p+1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-2p)\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 2+(2p+1)\\cdot (-20) \\\\  & =6-12p-8-40p-20 \\\\  & =-52p-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-126,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-52p-22 & =-126 \\\\ -52p & =-104 \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0227bc7e-d685-5eb6-939f-5a01c324b026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702208} {:answer/id #uuid "062003e6-95bf-52bb-baef-87af08c37cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{17}{46}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702210} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1de013-5fd5-5143-bf5a-d428a8910393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{46}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702213} {:answer/id #uuid "5674f606-9746-582e-8787-06fae88e667f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702218} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6e89e5-bf1e-53cb-b02d-5eb55a84aeab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e1de013-5fd5-5143-bf5a-d428a8910393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{46}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702213} :answer-field/id #uuid "191fd38b-2d03-5167-adae-cae0a939b28a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702212}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4286bde8-6293-54c6-a779-7a01b005727a" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1 - 2 p & 5 & 2 p + 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nis $-38,$  find the value of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(1 - 2 p)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1 - 2 p)((3)(2)-(0)(-2)) \\\\  & =(1 - 2 p)(6) \\\\  & =6 - 12 p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(5)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(5)((1)(2)-(0)(5)) \\\\  & =-(5)(2) \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(2 p + 1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 p + 1)((1)(-2)-(3)(5)) \\\\  & =(2 p + 1)(-17) \\\\  & =- 34 p - 17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =- 46 p - 21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the determinant equal to the given value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 46 p - 21 & =-38 \\\\ - 46 p & =-17 \\\\ p & =\\frac{17}{46}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=\\frac{17}{46}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f912c0e-d287-5eac-9cc6-bf5595ee0621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{64}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702225} {:answer/id #uuid "a2642eb2-2c52-5d3f-bdfc-d67b3e491a9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702226} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1d1a6-a72f-5b04-b706-26c401d4a6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702235} {:answer/id #uuid "dca7faab-be12-5ec6-8c1e-c5aa8bf517b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702236} {:answer/id #uuid "edec8f1e-ed05-570a-bf71-a6069f3eb632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f912c0e-d287-5eac-9cc6-bf5595ee0621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{64}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702225} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c087f21-8e66-5a8a-a89c-7842e1a09466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702217}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd2949b5-dacf-54db-85a1-9dea06bbf3d8" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 k + 1 & 3 & k \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)((3)(1)-(k)(0)) \\\\  & =(-1)(3) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & k \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1)((2 k + 1)(1)-(k)(-5)) \\\\  & =-(1)(7 k + 1) \\\\  & =- 7 k - 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-4)((2 k + 1)(0)-(3)(-5)) \\\\  & =(-4)(15) \\\\  & =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =- 7 k - 64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 7 k - 64 & =0 \\\\ - 7 k & =64 \\\\ k & =- \\frac{64}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=- \\frac{64}{7}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb8d5f1-e706-5323-8c8f-14ff06591a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702211} {:answer/id #uuid "6a727532-45a1-5be4-aea1-dcb6e07446d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702219} {:answer/id #uuid "cc266b5f-2b9b-5e4f-9a19-04e629103fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702230} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae454c-7621-568b-89e6-816ea80f6e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{37}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702233} {:answer/id #uuid "fc555972-cd60-5717-aacc-23a96420df87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{47}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae454c-7621-568b-89e6-816ea80f6e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{37}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702233} :answer-field/id #uuid "b00de1cb-feca-5d11-886d-c45b2091bc4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702227}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0a66ca1-e7f8-58ff-87f8-fbd4e590ca05" :question/problem "Given that \n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nand $det(C)=-20,$ find the value of $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(2)\\begin{vmatrix}q & 5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2)((q)(1)-(5)(-2)) \\\\  & =(2)(q + 10) \\\\  & =2 q + 20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(-5)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-5)((-1)(1)-(5)(0)) \\\\  & =-(-5)(-1) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)((-1)(-2)-(q)(0)) \\\\  & =(1)(2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 q + 17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the determinant equal to the given value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 q + 17 & =-20 \\\\ 2 q & =-37 \\\\ q & =- \\frac{37}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $q=- \\frac{37}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c52eb1-dc93-5f62-b593-84edcb93caf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702209} {:answer/id #uuid "95ee1035-3b87-56e4-ab21-928fcc409ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702223} {:answer/id #uuid "96bf0a1b-1970-5070-acd0-dd618a6b6bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702224} {:answer/id #uuid "c69cbe1a-4074-5045-9635-8e7c332178b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702229} {:answer/id #uuid "f900eb6b-5591-55dd-9655-25858be26923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c69cbe1a-4074-5045-9635-8e7c332178b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702229} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd4e691-7e81-5f27-bdff-2f4705d6d80d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702222}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6547f0c-f724-5854-949b-655cae6b55c2" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 k + 1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)((3)(1)-(k)(0)) \\\\  & =(-3)(3) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & k \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-2)((2 k + 1)(1)-(k)(1)) \\\\  & =-(-2)(k + 1) \\\\  & =2 k + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}2 k + 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-4)((2 k + 1)(0)-(3)(1)) \\\\  & =(-4)(-3) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 k + 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 k + 5 & =0 \\\\ 2 k & =-5 \\\\ k & =- \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=- \\frac{5}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468b982b-642a-5d50-a1df-99188a41f00d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702215} {:answer/id #uuid "4927d35d-4bc6-5d7f-9f04-43cfcb4b8ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702216} {:answer/id #uuid "842d4bbc-062c-512a-88ad-b8b1603e5b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702220} {:answer/id #uuid "84a14750-ec19-5110-ad4a-520f0a6e72bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702221} {:answer/id #uuid "ee38bff1-f26b-55dd-8bf9-1c3b2a7a0e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "842d4bbc-062c-512a-88ad-b8b1603e5b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702220} :answer-field/id #uuid "d15386a3-0a85-595c-8df3-84e439cd8766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4b3cff5-a90f-51c6-a399-b775816b7817" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $x$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & - x\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(3)\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & - x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3)((-3)(- x)-(2)(-1)) \\\\  & =(3)(3 x + 2) \\\\  & =9 x + 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(4)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ x & - x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(4)((1)(- x)-(2)(x)) \\\\  & =-(4)(- 3 x) \\\\  & =12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(8)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ x & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(8)((1)(-1)-(-3)(x)) \\\\  & =(8)(3 x - 1) \\\\  & =24 x - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =45 x - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}45 x - 2 & =0 \\\\ 45 x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{45}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{2}{45}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eeee876-ea72-52e0-aaea-9bffd896b2ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705289} {:answer/id #uuid "b58dc4a7-a1dd-5b86-bb15-a5b7b753ba83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705295} {:answer/id #uuid "b8317694-36cb-5e28-ab58-4c2875782073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705296} {:answer/id #uuid "c410ebc6-e22a-5175-a85d-358914011d9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and $4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705297} {:answer/id #uuid "e4da1484-aa24-5f55-a40f-2a25c854f291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b58dc4a7-a1dd-5b86-bb15-a5b7b753ba83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705295} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dcec67b-11e2-5e44-9cda-f08fcea7fea4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705283}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08a89fa1-a53d-5ad3-97c9-5f44159c8118" :question/problem "Find all real values of $p$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ - 3 p - 4 & 4 p + 7 & - 3 p - 3 \\\\ - 5 p - 8 & 6 p + 13 & - 5 p - 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}4 p + 7 & - 3 p - 3 \\\\ 6 p + 13 & - 5 p - 9\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)((4 p + 7)(- 5 p - 9)-(- 3 p - 3)(6 p + 13)) \\\\  & =(1)(- 2 p^{2} - 14 p - 24) \\\\  & =- 2 p^{2} - 14 p - 24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}- 3 p - 4 & - 3 p - 3 \\\\ - 5 p - 8 & - 5 p - 9\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-2)((- 3 p - 4)(- 5 p - 9)-(- 3 p - 3)(- 5 p - 8)) \\\\  & =-(-2)(8 p + 12) \\\\  & =16 p + 24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(2)\\begin{vmatrix}- 3 p - 4 & 4 p + 7 \\\\ - 5 p - 8 & 6 p + 13\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2)((- 3 p - 4)(6 p + 13)-(4 p + 7)(- 5 p - 8)) \\\\  & =(2)(2 p^{2} + 4 p + 4) \\\\  & =4 p^{2} + 8 p + 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 p^{2} + 10 p + 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 p^{2} + 10 p + 8 & =0 \\\\ 2 (p + 1) (p + 4) & =0 \\\\ p & =-4,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p=-4$ and $p=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "163fe3c5-117c-50d3-b4e4-1e1ab7ad0456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705277} {:answer/id #uuid "278180ec-78bd-5264-b491-657694531bf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705279} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba48029-fb1a-5102-bac0-61297b575932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705288} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a3c725-28b3-5c88-8b27-cf22ec5c389d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ and $2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705292} {:answer/id #uuid "dc554ed9-06e6-50ac-af73-df339c379c7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "163fe3c5-117c-50d3-b4e4-1e1ab7ad0456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705277} :answer-field/id #uuid "9682fd7b-3892-5768-8819-c647568b313a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "85af9268-b852-5f3d-84a0-5ddde79250a5" :question/problem "Find all real values of $p$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}- p - 2 & - 2 p - 3 & p + 1 \\\\ 3 p + 3 & 4 p + 7 & - 3 p - 5 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(- p - 2)\\begin{vmatrix}4 p + 7 & - 3 p - 5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(- p - 2)((4 p + 7)(2)-(- 3 p - 5)(-2)) \\\\  & =(- p - 2)(2 p + 4) \\\\  & =- 2 p^{2} - 8 p - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(- 2 p - 3)\\begin{vmatrix}3 p + 3 & - 3 p - 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(- 2 p - 3)((3 p + 3)(2)-(- 3 p - 5)(-1)) \\\\  & =-(- 2 p - 3)(3 p + 1) \\\\  & =6 p^{2} + 11 p + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(p + 1)\\begin{vmatrix}3 p + 3 & 4 p + 7 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(p + 1)((3 p + 3)(-2)-(4 p + 7)(-1)) \\\\  & =(p + 1)(1 - 2 p) \\\\  & =- 2 p^{2} - p + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 p^{2} + 2 p - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 p^{2} + 2 p - 4 & =0 \\\\ 2 (p - 1) (p + 2) & =0 \\\\ p & =-2,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p=-2$ and $p=1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1541c782-1eb4-5ec0-9322-8520916fd484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705276} {:answer/id #uuid "26126201-c1f2-5abe-a041-50e7fbd8ba7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705278} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb0b957-012c-5eca-9568-4b483ff395a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ and $4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705284} {:answer/id #uuid "98dfc3d5-043c-5b2e-9cc9-d096d0e3a9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705291} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0aae61-15f0-50e9-b4b9-f63acd7eb26c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1541c782-1eb4-5ec0-9322-8520916fd484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705276} :answer-field/id #uuid "31a4fc94-2a07-5a72-9b1c-b56a92072074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705281}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "869472d3-d923-5499-8798-74bf41a36e0a" :question/problem "Find all real values of $p$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 p - 1 & p & p + 2 \\\\ 2 p - 1 & 1 - p & - p \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(- 2 p - 1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 - p & - p \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(- 2 p - 1)((1 - p)(2)-(- p)(1)) \\\\  & =(- 2 p - 1)(2 - p) \\\\  & =2 p^{2} - 3 p - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(p)\\begin{vmatrix}2 p - 1 & - p \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(p)((2 p - 1)(2)-(- p)(-2)) \\\\  & =-(p)(2 p - 2) \\\\  & =- 2 p^{2} + 2 p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(p + 2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 p - 1 & 1 - p \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(p + 2)((2 p - 1)(1)-(1 - p)(-2)) \\\\  & =(p + 2)(1) \\\\  & =p + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant is $0$ for every real value of $p$. Therefore, the matrix is singular for every real value of $p$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5be13b03-5b80-500d-8b75-064858690378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705282} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ad5c23-8bd9-53aa-a17e-08702a71de72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705293} {:answer/id #uuid "b58d939e-b8d3-5fa6-a73c-19864c42aaac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705294} {:answer/id #uuid "e374ec34-e113-5dee-9eac-36b84549986f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705299} {:answer/id #uuid "ee05a336-ebc8-5ca9-8ba3-8387290a4d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and $2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e374ec34-e113-5dee-9eac-36b84549986f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705299} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf63112-d210-58cb-911f-c3cc2e1b3a7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705280}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8730b36b-1834-5182-9c12-0cd8c03fa744" :question/problem "Find all real values of $p$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 p & - p - 1 & 1 - p \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 p - 5 & 4 - p & 3 - p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(2 p)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 - p & 3 - p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 p)((2)(3 - p)-(1)(4 - p)) \\\\  & =(2 p)(2 - p) \\\\  & =- 2 p^{2} + 4 p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(- p - 1)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 p - 5 & 3 - p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(- p - 1)((-2)(3 - p)-(1)(2 p - 5)) \\\\  & =-(- p - 1)(-1) \\\\  & =- p - 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(1 - p)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 p - 5 & 4 - p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1 - p)((-2)(4 - p)-(2)(2 p - 5)) \\\\  & =(1 - p)(2 - 2 p) \\\\  & =2 p^{2} - 4 p + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =1 - p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA singular matrix has determinant $0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 - p & =0 \\\\ - p & =-1 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=1$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}]}
